            <ArticleTitle>Intravenous drug abuse mimicking vasculitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>505-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>&quot;Mimickers&quot; of vasculitis are well-documented in the literature. We report a case of intravenous drug abuse manifesting with signs and symptoms suggestive of vasculitis. This case highlights the need for diagnostic precision in the evaluation of suspected vasculitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
